WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/components/feedback/InlineCallout.tsx. A single-line, low-chrome callout that surfaces one actionable
  insight inside a larger card (e.g. "1 anomaly in this range — Apr 24 →"). It is a PURE presentational
  primitive — no hooks, no TanStack queries, no t() calls (the prompt's "Data sources: (none)" / "i18n keys:
  (none extracted)" / "Shared components used: (none)" / "pure presentational component"). Its branches:

    type CalloutVariant = 'info' | 'success' | 'warning' | 'danger'
    VARIANT_STYLES[variant] = { bg (tint fill), ring (1px border), text (body colour), iconText (icon+action) }
      info    : bg-cyan-500/5     ring-cyan-400/20     text-[--text-secondary]  iconText-cyan-300
      success : bg-emerald-500/5  ring-emerald-400/20  text-[--text-secondary]  iconText-emerald-300
      warning : bg-amber-500/5    ring-amber-400/25    text-amber-200/85        iconText-amber-300
      danger  : bg-rose-500/5     ring-rose-400/25     text-rose-200/85         iconText-rose-300
    Props   : variant, icon? (ReactNode), children (body), action? {label, href?, onClick?}, className?, testId?
    content : [icon span (h-4 w-4, iconText)] + [body span (text-xs, flex-1 min-w-0, text)]
              + [action span (text-xs font-medium, iconText): {label}<ChevronRight h-3 w-3/>]
    baseClass: inline-flex w-full items-center gap-2 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 ring-1 transition-colors + bg + ring
               + (interactive ? hover:bg-white/[0.03] focus-visible:ring-2 ring-cyan-400/60 : '')
    render  : action.href  → <a href> (navigation, prefers href when both given)
              action.onClick→ <button>
              neither       → <div role="status">
  i18n     : the source is "anonymous" — it has NO hardcoded prose (body + action label are caller-supplied).
             The only native-owned strings are the VoiceOver severity words, promoted to P1/S10 keys (table
             "InlineCallout") so the Swift sources hold no English prose literals.

