PARITY MAPPING  (web → Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind ported, no raw hex)
  CalloutVariant info/success/warning/danger → Color.TS.statusInfo / statusSuccess / statusWarning / statusDanger
  bg-{c}-500/5                 → statusColor.opacity(0.05)                     (InlineCalloutStyle.fillOpacity)
  ring-{c}-400/20|25           → statusColor.opacity(0.20 info+success | 0.25 warning+danger) 1pt strokeBorder
  text (body)                  → textSecondary for info+success; statusColor for warning+danger (web tinted text)
  iconText (icon + action)     → statusColor (InlineCalloutStyle.accent)
  rounded-lg / gap-2           → TSRadius.sm (8) / TSSpacing.sm (8)
  px-3 py-2                    → .padding(.horizontal TSSpacing.md=12, .vertical TSSpacing.sm=8)
  lucide icon (h-4 w-4)        → Image(systemName:) 16pt, caller-supplied SF Symbol (web icon is caller-supplied)
  ChevronRight (h-3 w-3)       → Image(systemName: "chevron.right") 12pt, accessibilityHidden
  <a href>/<button>/role=status→ Link / Button(+InlineCalloutButtonStyle) / combined static a11y element
  hover:bg-white/[0.03] active → InlineCalloutButtonStyle scrim Color.primary.opacity(.03 hover / .06 pressed),
                                 animated via TSMotion.fastDuration unless Reduce Motion (web transition-colors)
  focus-visible:ring          → default platform focus ring (macOS / hardware keyboard)
  data-testid                  → .accessibilityIdentifier (only when supplied)
  className                    → dropped (Tailwind class string is not portable; documented)
  i18n                         → severity words via InlineCalloutStrings (NSLocalizedString table "InlineCallout",
                                 web English as value: fallback)
  a11y                         → VoiceOver label "{Severity}: {message}[. {actionLabel}]"; icon + chevron hidden;
                                 Dynamic Type via Font.TS; Reduce Motion respected in the interactive scrim
  telemetry                    → view.opened surface="InlineCallout" emitted once on first appear (P1/S11)

STATES (every branch in the source reproduced — no hidden surface)
  The web source is purely presentational, so it has NO loading / empty / error / stale / offline data axis to
  reproduce (the generic prompt template lists those, but this artifact's metadata is explicit: "pure
  presentational component", Data sources "(none)"). Inventing data-driven states for a stateless primitive would
  be scope drift. The source's REAL branches are reproduced in full and exercised by previews + tests:
    variant      → info / success / warning / danger (tint, ring, body, accent each asserted).
    render mode  → link (href) / button (onClick) / status (neither) — InlineCalloutRenderMode.resolve asserted.
    icon         → present (leading SF Symbol) / absent.
    action       → present (label + chevron, interactive scrim + focus ring) / absent (static role=status).
    content      → plain String message and arbitrary rich content (both initializers).

